			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance submodules — Decouple Mountain via Air, Vine, and Cache delegation\n\nAdvance 11 Element submodules to modularize the Mountain backend and finalize the gRPC communication surface for the Air daemon and Cocoon extension host.\n\nMountain (refactor): Systematically delegate gRPC client logic, Cocoon notification handlers, and caching mechanisms to the dedicated Air, Vine, and Cache crates. Replace local implementations for AssetMemoryMap, PathCanon, and Vine connectivity with thin compatibility shims, significantly reducing Mountain's internal code surface.\n\nAir (feat): Implement 14 domain methods in the AirClient (ApplyUpdate, Authenticate, etc.) and introduce the AirServiceProvider façade. This provides a high-level, thread-safe gRPC orchestration layer with automated RequestID generation and ergonomic response normalization.\n\nVine (feat + refactor): Implement a comprehensive suite of Cocoon notification handlers featuring a \"channel-drain\" coalescing pattern. High-frequency events like ProgressReport and SetTextEditorDecorations are now batched within 16-50ms temporal windows to preserve Sky renderer performance under heavy extension load.\n\nCache (feat): Add the Cache element as a standalone submodule to centralize asset mapping and path canonicalization logic previously housed within Mountain.\n\nOutput (fix): Refactor window management commands to use the typed Tauri 2 window API, ensuring native drag and maximize operations work reliably in the Sky renderer.\n\nOther: Advance pointers for Cocoon (RouteManifest), SideCar (lint suppressions), and routine dependency bumps for Common, Echo, and Sky.",
			"SHA": "711d768c81882601b714ba177b8030f0ab8f98a8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T09:57:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Air submodule — gRPC client foundation, DTO atoms, and client scaffold\n\nProgress Air-Client Phase 2 synthesis per Mountain-Crate-Split plan. Port `AirClient` struct, async connect, and thread-safe `Arc<Mutex<>>` wrapper from Mountain. Land nine atomized DTO types (`AirMetrics`, `AirStatus`, `DownloadStreamChunk`, `ExtendedFileInfo`, `FileInfo`, `FileResult`, `IndexInfo`, `ResourceUsage`, `UpdateInfo`) plus the `DownloadStream` async-iterator adapter. Wire `Source/Client/mod.rs` into `Source/Library.rs` and introduce `DEFAULT_AIR_SERVER_ADDRESS` constant.\n\nDomain method stubs (`authenticate`, `check_for_update`, `download_file`, etc.) still live in Mountain; this commit establishes the canonical crate surface for downstream consumption.",
			"SHA": "9bbc56a70d1fc9518a184629f832742ab6b7831d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T09:55:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance submodules — Vine crate split, Mountain capability sync, Air re-export cleanup\n\nAdvance three Element submodules that progressively decouple Vine from Mountain and harden Tauri window management.\n\nVine (`feat`): Bootstrap the first two phases of the Mountain-Crate-Split plan. Phase 1 extracts the in-tree gRPC protocol into a standalone workspace crate with three cargo features (`client`, `server`, `multiplexer`), a complete `Proto/Vine.proto` surface, and fourteen atomized client entry points. Phase 2 populates the previously-empty server module with constants, validation helpers, graceful-shutdown bind tasks, and nine renderer-event relay atoms. The crate now compiles independently and exposes both client and server surfaces, unblocking downstream consumption in Mountain and Air.\n\nMountain (`fix`): Regenerate `gen/schemas/capabilities.json` from the source-of-truth default manifest so the capability digest includes window management permissions (`start-dragging`, `toggle-maximize`, `close`, etc.). This resolves Tauri runtime validation rejections that were breaking interactive titlebar operations from Sky.\n\nAir (`refactor` + `style`): Replace the local `VineError` definition with a re-export of `Element/Vine::VineError`, add an `AirCompat` shim for backward-compatible constructors, and follow-up with a rustfmt formatting pass. This eliminates error-type duplication and aligns Air with the canonical Vine crate.",
			"SHA": "c171f4fb30db3556f96b6373cc3cc0d056e53ec7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T18:31:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Common): Advance Documentation/Rust submodule pointer\n\nUpdate the Common crate's Documentation/Rust submodule from 14a0ed4c to 98c2f81f, pulling in the latest Rust documentation updates for the Common crate's trait and type references.\n\nThis keeps the in-repo documentation aligned with the upstream documentation source.",
			"SHA": "723ece27a0181c0b4e9dc3e77a2e6e07f9705814"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
